msgid "Settings for API client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The public ebarimt info endpoints (district codes, TIN info, merchant info, product tax codes, "
"BÜNA classification) do not require auth, so every credential field below is optional, and the "
"client never sends a token or API key to those endpoints."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The credentials are used only by ``merchant_registration`` (``saveOprMerchants``), which needs an"
" OAuth2 password-grant token (``token_url``, ``client_id``, ``username``, ``password``; "
"``client_secret`` and ``scope`` when the realm requires them) and an ``api_key`` sent as ``X-API-"
"KEY``."
msgstr ""

msgid "True when every field a password-grant token request needs is set."
msgstr ""

msgid "Names of the required password-grant fields that are not set."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration for transport retry behaviour."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Retries apply only to requests whose HTTP method is in ``retry_methods``; any other method is "
"sent exactly once regardless of ``max_retries``. Opt a non-idempotent method in explicitly if "
"your deployment guarantees it is safe, e.g. ``retry_methods=RetrySettings.DEFAULT_RETRY_METHODS |"
" {\"POST\"}``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Backoff is exponential (``backoff_base_seconds * 2**attempt``) capped at ``max_backoff_seconds``,"
" with *full jitter* (uniform in ``[0, backoff]``) when ``jitter`` is on, so a fleet of POS "
"devices that fail together does not retry in lockstep. A ``Retry-After`` header from the server, "
"when ``respect_retry_after`` is on, replaces the computed backoff (still capped)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``retry_unsent`` (off by default) lets methods outside ``retry_methods`` (``POST``/``PATCH``, "
"e.g. ``receipt.create``) be re-sent, but only after a failure that proves the request never left "
"the client: connection refused, DNS failure, connect timeout, or a proxy that refused the tunnel "
"(see ``PosApiTransportError.request_sent``). Such a request cannot have been persisted, so re-"
"sending it cannot duplicate a write. Responses (including 5xx) and failures after the request may"
" have been sent (read timeout, dropped connection, ...) are still never retried for those "
"methods."
msgstr ""

msgid "Return True if requests with this HTTP method may be re-sent."
msgstr ""

msgid "Upper bound on attempts the transport may make for ``method``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``max_retries`` for retryable methods, and for any method when ``retry_unsent`` is on (those "
"extra attempts are only used after a never-sent failure, see ``may_retry``); exactly 1 otherwise."
msgstr ""

msgid "Return True if a failed attempt of ``method`` may be re-sent."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``request_sent`` is ``False`` only when the failure proves the request never reached the server; "
"pass ``True`` for an HTTP response."
msgstr ""

msgid "Return the sleep duration before the next retry."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``attempt`` is the 0-based index of the attempt that just failed. ``retry_after`` is the server-"
"requested delay in seconds (already parsed from a ``Retry-After`` header), or ``None`` if absent."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ebarimt api settings factory."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The public ebarimt info endpoints don't require OAuth2, so credentials are optional. They are "
"used only by ``merchant_registration``, which needs ``client_id``, ``username``, ``password`` and"
" ``api_key`` (the environment's ``X-API-KEY``); the token URL comes from the preset."
msgstr ""

